        "id": 7555
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-14T02:50:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t this method be checking m.certState first? To avoid deserializing the cert repeatedly during the happy path.\n\nI imagine the overall flow should be something like:\na) check in memory certs, if its there, block on verification completing, then return it.\nb) try and load from the cache; if found, populate the in-memory certs, and return it.\nc) check in memory certs again, if its there, block on verification completing and return it. If its not there, create it, and kickoff acme.",
      "revId": "0c3b50398588ef127faada1e8521bc5bf192a26a",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
